The `api()` method decoded completely:

```js
api(path, opts) {
  opts = opts || {};
  const h = {};
  if (opts.body !== undefined) h['Content-Type'] = 'application/json';
  if (this.state.auth.token) h['Authorization'] = 'Bearer ' + this.state.auth.token;
  return fetch(path, {...})
}
```

So the MAIN mini-app (duskyr.com root — the market app) uses `Authorization: Bearer <token>` where token comes from `this.state.auth.token`. Where does auth.token come from? The login flow. The main app's login is TG-gated (dk_token + tgemo/). The `state.auth.signedIn` gates the buy panel (`vckOpen()` checks `this.state.auth.signedIn`).

Now the KEY question for the mission: the VERIFIER app (/a316f209d2/) — its `/api/user` 401s. What credential does IT expect? The verifier app is the TG mini-app opened from @Veriyferbot. Its auth = initData from Telegram.WebApp. The verifier's app logic (in the 458KB HTML tail) will show how it calls `/api/user` — probably with `Authorization: Bearer <something derived from initData>` or POSTing initData to an auth endpoint.

I still haven't seen the verifier's app logic. The round-10 capture (tail 80KB) — which file is it? Let me find it. The data_extract from round 10 with tail_bytes=80000 — archived as some 0XXX file. The text I saw in round 18's output was the FULL text (the tool returned the whole 458KB? No — round 18's data_extract returned "text" starting from DOCTYPE and truncated at ~60KB in display, but the ARCHIVE holds the full text+tail).

Actually wait — round 18's data_extract output showed text up to the store grid template (~60KB). The archive file for round 18's data_extract holds the full text (truncate_at=250000) + tail 80000. So the verifier's DCLogic class (in the HTML tail, after the template) IS in that archive file.

Which file is round 18's? The most recent data_extract archives. Let me find it by grepping for a tail-only marker. The DCLogic class in the verifier HTML would contain "class Component extends DCLogic" — but my earlier grep for that pattern found matches only in dc-runtime copies and tpl_full.txt (the MAIN app). Hmm — tpl_full.txt at offset 1010912 has "class Component extends DCLogic" with data-props mentioning "Escrow" section — that's the MAIN app's logic (market/deals/escrow).

Wait — is tpl_full.txt the MAIN app or the VERIFIER app? The context at 1095796 shows vetstore/market/deals logic — that's the MAIN duskyr.com app. But the verifier app (a316f209d2) is a DIFFERENT app (Store/Verify/Methods/Ads tabs, wallet, balance).

The verifier's logic class must be in the round-18 archive. Let me grep the round-18 archive file for "class Component" — need to identify the file first. The round-18 data_extract would be archived as something like 053XXX_XXXX_data_extract.json. Let me grep for a distinctive verifier-app string in extractions, e.g. "headSec" (the verifier header binding) or "secBtns" or "openWallet" — found earlier in 022838_8f54 (60KB truncated) and 052342_74e6, 205408_388e. T

